##Day- 5
#Assignment-02: Your Own Task, Walked and Improved

##Easy 
1. Why should a student turn the seven task-path answers into one clear message?
ANS: A student should turn the seven task-path answers into one clear message because it helps the AI understand the task properly. 
It includes the purpose, important facts, instructions, and expected result. This reduces confusion and helps the student get a more useful and accurate answer.
2. What does it mean to find one weak step in a first attempt?
Finding one weak step means identifying the part of the task where the first attempt went wrong or lacked important information. 
Instead of repeating the entire task, we should correct that particular step and improve the result.
3. Why is “it looks fine” not enough before trusting an AI answer?
“It looks fine” is not enough because an AI answer may contain incorrect facts or miss important details. We should check the result against our actual 
requirements and verify important information before trusting or using it.

##Intermediate 
4. A student asks, “Help me with my assignment.” The result is too general. Which task-path step is weak? What should the student add?
The “What do you give the assistant?” step is weak because the student has not provided enough information. The student should add the assignment topic,
 specific questions, relevant notes, required format, and expected length. This helps the AI provide a more specific and useful answer.
5. A student gets a revision timetable but never checks whether the daily workload fits their real pace. What human step did they skip?
The student skipped the “decide yourself” step. They should review the timetable and decide whether the daily workload suits their learning speed, available time, 
and other activities. They should also check whether the schedule is realistic before following it.

##Hard
6. Choose one real task you need this week. Write a clear message for an AI tool using purpose, useful facts, task, and expected result.
My Task: Preparing a Revision Timetable for an Exam
I have an upcoming exam and need a practical revision timetable for one subject. I will provide the subject name, important topics, 
the number of days remaining, and the time I can study each day. Please prepare a simple daily timetable that covers all the important topics, 
includes short breaks, and provides time for revision and practice questions. I expect a clear, realistic schedule that I can follow easily.
 After receiving the timetable, I will decide whether it suits my daily routine and check whether all the topics are included.
7. Your first result is off-target. Name one weak step you would fix, what you would change, and what you would check in the new result.
If my first result is off-target, I would fix the “What do you give the assistant?” step. I would provide more accurate details about the topics,
 days remaining, and available study hours. Then, I would ask the AI to prepare a revised timetable based on these details.
In the new result, I would check whether all the topics are covered, the daily workload is manageable, and enough time is available for revision and practice. I would make my own final decision before following the timetable.